They say the kind of things

1445
00:54:41,120 --> 00:54:42,640
you'd actually hear

1446
00:54:42,640 --> 00:54:43,480
from your friends.

1447
00:54:43,480 --> 00:54:44,280
Yeah.

1448
00:54:48,000 --> 00:54:49,240
Should we go?

1449
00:54:49,240 --> 00:54:49,960
She's asleep.

1450
00:54:49,960 --> 00:54:51,360
Should we go to the gym

1451
00:54:51,360 --> 00:54:52,640
and punch some holes?

1452
00:54:52,640 --> 00:54:53,400
Sure.

1453
00:54:59,580 --> 00:55:03,780
(Carefully picks it up)

1454
00:55:03,820 --> 00:55:06,140
(Tiptoes around)

1455
00:55:06,540 --> 00:55:07,860
(Looks back)
Aw, that's sweet.

1456
00:55:10,880 --> 00:55:12,200
Let's go. It's okay.

1457
00:55:12,200 --> 00:55:15,440
Let her get some good sleep.

1458
00:55:15,720 --> 00:55:18,400
She barely slept last night.

1459
00:55:19,480 --> 00:55:20,520
She was up all night.

1460
00:55:26,840 --> 00:55:28,120
We can punch the hole here.

1461
00:55:28,120 --> 00:55:29,760
Right in this corner.

1462
00:55:29,760 --> 00:55:30,560
Okay.

1463
00:55:30,560 --> 00:55:31,640
Let's each punch a hole in the corner.

1464
00:55:31,640 --> 00:55:31,920
Okay.

1465
00:55:32,720 --> 00:55:34,800
We really
do have a lot going on every day.

1466
00:55:47,980 --> 00:55:48,830
Oh my gosh.

1467
00:55:53,680 --> 00:55:54,560
What is she doing?

1468
00:55:54,560 --> 00:55:55,560
What's going on?

1469
00:55:56,280 --> 00:55:57,280
That scared me.

1470
00:55:59,280 --> 00:56:00,360
Work on your thesis.

1471
00:56:01,520 --> 00:56:02,400
Don't worry about me.

1472
00:56:13,680 --> 00:56:14,600
Teacher.

1473
00:56:18,400 --> 00:56:19,530
Sha Yue'er is waking up.

1474
00:56:30,480 --> 00:56:31,720
Help me out here.

1475
00:56:31,720 --> 00:56:32,680
Why am I here?

1476
00:56:37,240 --> 00:56:38,200
Thanks, guys.

1477
00:56:38,200 --> 00:56:39,640
You're even whispering.

1478
00:56:40,160 --> 00:56:41,040
It's no trouble.

1479
00:56:41,040 --> 00:56:43,000
We always talk this quietly.

1480
00:56:43,400 --> 00:56:44,720
I'm going back to bed.

1481
00:56:47,960 --> 00:56:48,920
Bye.

1482
00:56:48,920 --> 00:56:49,560
Good luck, guys.

1483
00:56:49,560 --> 00:56:50,600
You're going to bed?

1484
00:56:50,600 --> 00:56:51,600
Yeah.

1485
00:57:06,100 --> 00:57:08,900
(Opens her eyes)

1486
00:57:08,900 --> 00:57:10,360
She's got too much on her mind to sleep.

1487
00:57:13,680 --> 00:57:14,440
She seems

1488
00:57:14,440 --> 00:57:15,680
a little defeated right now.

1489
00:57:17,080 --> 00:57:19,120
She's been pretty down tonight.

1490
00:57:19,600 --> 00:57:21,040
She was

1491
00:57:21,600 --> 00:57:22,400
expecting

1492
00:57:22,400 --> 00:57:23,640
a big date

1493
00:57:23,640 --> 00:57:24,440
today.

1494
00:57:24,440 --> 00:57:26,280
She just let
her emotions get the better of her.

1495
00:57:26,280 --> 00:57:27,680
She probably knows

1496
00:57:27,680 --> 00:57:28,840
she wasn't

1497
00:57:28,840 --> 00:57:30,520
thinking clearly either.

1498
00:57:30,520 --> 00:57:31,640
Things just kept escalating.

1499
00:57:31,640 --> 00:57:32,360
But it's

1500
00:57:32,360 --> 00:57:33,160
happened.

1501
00:57:33,160 --> 00:57:33,720
Yeah.

1502
00:57:33,920 --> 00:57:34,840
Still, it's a shame.

1503
00:57:34,840 --> 00:57:35,720
This time was

1504
00:57:35,720 --> 00:57:36,840
supposed to be a real date.

1505
00:57:36,840 --> 00:57:38,240
While everyone else was going on dates,

1506
00:57:38,240 --> 00:57:38,960
she missed

1507
00:57:38,960 --> 00:57:39,320
this one.

1508
00:57:39,320 --> 00:57:40,440
It wasn't just this one.

1509
00:57:40,440 --> 00:57:42,000
She missed both big dates.

1510
00:57:42,000 --> 00:57:43,080
(Missed both dates)
They both missed them.

1511
00:57:43,080 --> 00:57:44,280
All they got was the stargazing room.

1512
00:57:44,280 --> 00:57:44,640
Right.

1513
00:57:44,840 --> 00:57:45,680
Other than the stargazing room,

1514
00:57:45,680 --> 00:57:47,280
they haven't had a real date.

1515
00:57:47,960 --> 00:57:48,720
Their timing

1516
00:57:49,320 --> 00:57:50,400
is always off.

1517
00:57:51,000 --> 00:57:51,960
Everyone else gets little

1518
00:57:51,960 --> 00:57:52,800
conversations and interactions,

1519
00:57:52,800 --> 00:57:54,160
then makes a big leap when it

1520
00:57:54,160 --> 00:57:54,920
really matters.

1521
00:57:54,920 --> 00:57:55,840
But with these two,

1522
00:57:55,840 --> 00:57:56,880
whenever they reach a turning point,

1523
00:57:56,880 --> 00:57:58,320
they start poking at each other,

1524
00:57:58,320 --> 00:57:59,560
testing each other, doing all this...

1525
00:58:00,320 --> 00:58:02,360
It feels like they're
actually drifting farther apart.

1526
00:58:02,360 --> 00:58:02,800
She's

1527
00:58:02,800 --> 00:58:03,480
someone who's

1528
00:58:03,480 --> 00:58:04,640
afraid of being abandoned.

1529
00:58:04,920 --> 00:58:05,360
Right?

1530
00:58:05,360 --> 00:58:06,720
She needs a lot of reassurance.

1531
00:58:06,720 --> 00:58:07,200
And being in this

1532
00:58:07,200 --> 00:58:08,720
environment probably makes

1533
00:58:08,720 --> 00:58:10,680
those feelings even stronger.

1534
00:58:11,680 --> 00:58:12,320
I think this

1535
00:58:12,320 --> 00:58:13,200
has gotta hurt.

1536
00:58:13,200 --> 00:58:14,960
Without this happening,

1537
00:58:14,960 --> 00:58:17,280
